From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XuanTie Linux SDK CI <noreply@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Sun, 3 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] six: add find_spec to vendored six importer for Python 3.13

mozjs-91 ships a tree copy of six (third_party/python/six/six.py,
1.13.0) that is put on PYTHONPATH for do_configure. configure.py imports
mozbuild, which does `from six.moves import builtins as __builtin__`.

six's _SixMetaPathImporter only implements the legacy find_module()/
load_module() finder protocol and has no find_spec(). Since CPython 3.12
the import system no longer falls back to a meta path finder's legacy
find_module() (importlib._bootstrap._find_spec only calls finder.find_spec
and skips finders lacking it). The six.moves virtual namespace therefore
never gets registered and configure fails on python3 3.13 with:

    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'six.moves'

Backport the fix upstream six shipped in 1.16.0: give the importer
find_spec()/create_module()/exec_module() (importlib Loader protocol) and
the spec_from_loader import. This restores the six.moves namespace instead
of rewriting each call site. Behaviour on Python <= 3.11 is unchanged
(spec_from_loader is imported defensively).

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/benjaminp/six commit 6c8dcc1 ; vendored copy]
---
--- a/third_party/python/six/six.py
+++ b/third_party/python/six/six.py
@@ -31,6 +31,11 @@
 __author__ = "Benjamin Peterson <benjamin@python.org>"
 __version__ = "1.13.0"

+try:
+    from importlib.util import spec_from_loader
+except ImportError:
+    spec_from_loader = None
+

 # Useful for very coarse version differentiation.
 PY2 = sys.version_info[0] == 2
@@ -186,6 +191,11 @@
             return self
         return None

+    def find_spec(self, fullname, path, target=None):
+        if fullname in self.known_modules:
+            return spec_from_loader(fullname, self)
+        return None
+
     def __get_module(self, fullname):
         try:
             return self.known_modules[fullname]
@@ -223,6 +233,12 @@
         return None
     get_source = get_code  # same as get_code

+    def create_module(self, spec):
+        return self.load_module(spec.name)
+
+    def exec_module(self, module):
+        pass
+
 _importer = _SixMetaPathImporter(__name__)

